---
/**
 * The label that follows the pointer across the industry panels, in place of
 * the arrow.
 *
 * The panels are links and the pointer should say where to. Purely decorative
 * duplication of what the panel already links to, so it is hidden from
 * assistive technology, and the `cursor: none` that hides the real arrow is
 * applied by script rather than in the stylesheet — a failed script leaves a
 * visible cursor rather than none at all.
 */
---

<div class="cursorpill" aria-hidden="true">
  Book a demo
  <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13">
    <path
      d="M3.2 8h9M8.6 4.4 12.2 8l-3.6 3.6"
      fill="none"
      stroke="currentColor"
      stroke-width="1.6"
      stroke-linecap="round"
      stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
  </svg>
</div>
